  "source_scope_note": "The selected problem is Proposition 2.6: uniform convergence, uniform module-dependent Lipschitz control and isogeny invariance of the renormalized Fargues polygons for finitely presented Breuil--Kisin--Fargues modules with M[1/pi] finite free. The exact finite p-adic field, perfectoid extension, ramified Witt ring, Frobenius and xi-prime localization hypotheses are retained; no finite-freeness or HN-type assumption is added. The complete author body retains all local torsion/quasi-abelian categories, devissage, rank/degree, polygon inequalities, convergence and isogeny error arguments. Named p-adic Hodge and category foundations remain explicit prerequisites; later tensor, Hodge, Tate and modification conclusions are unselected context.",
